  (testing "cloud-itonami-isic-5110, promoted to :implemented (AirlineOps-LLM / Aviation Safety Governor passenger-air-transport-operations-coordination actor, superproject ADR-2628000000; was :blueprint at the time of the corroboration list above -- superseded by its own dedicated corroboration block below)"
    (is (= :implemented (industry/maturity "5110"))))
  (testing "cloud-itonami-isic-4911, now implemented, is :implemented (live-state corroboration)"
    (is (= :implemented (industry/maturity "4911"))))
  (testing "cloud-itonami-isic-5011, promoted to :implemented by a CONCURRENT sibling fleet agent (not this promotion's own work -- corroborated here only to keep this shared hot test file truthful; live-state corroboration)"
    (is (= :implemented (industry/maturity "5011"))))
  (testing "cloud-itonami-isic-6020 (Television programming and broadcasting activities -- a PRE-EXISTING repository already at :blueprint tier [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md/CONTRIBUTING.md/GOVERNANCE.md/LICENSE/README.md/SECURITY.md/blueprint.edn/docs/ only, from an earlier bulk-scaffolding pass, no deps.edn/src/test] -- this work ADDED the missing deps.edn/src/test module set on top of that existing boilerplate rather than re-scaffolding; identity ({:id \"6020\" :name \"Television programming and broadcasting activities\"}) independently re-verified against a fresh clone before any work began, per this fleet's ID/name-mismatch caution; tvbroadcastops.* module (BroadcastOpsAdvisor ⊣ BroadcastLicenseGovernor, TV-broadcasting OPERATIONS COORDINATION actor, NOT direct on-air-content authority and NOT emergency-alert-broadcast authority) mirroring cloud-itonami-isic-5913's [Motion picture, video and television programme distribution activities] verified advisor/governor/phase/operation/store/sim module shape module-for-module (tvbroadcastops.* in place of filmdistops.*, station/license in place of title/contract); closed four-op allowlist, all :effect :propose (:log-broadcast-record/:schedule-broadcast-operation/:flag-content-concern/:coordinate-equipment-maintenance); HARD governor checks, all permanent and un-overridable by any human approval -- station-unverified (target station/license record must exist AND be independently :registered?/:verified? in the store before any proposal for it may commit or escalate), effect-not-propose, and scope-exclusion (folds in op-not-allowed) that permanently blocks any proposal touching finalization of an on-air-content decision or an emergency-alert-broadcast decision, per ADR-2607152500's Wave 4 person-facing-service guardrail; scope-excluded-terms are deliberately phrased as the finalization/execution ACTION (\"finalize the on-air content decision\", \"authorize the emergency alert broadcast\"), never a bare noun (\"content\"/\"broadcast\"/\"emergency alert\"), avoiding this fleet's own known self-tripping bug class, with a dedicated regression test (default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion in governor_test.clj) asserting all four default proposal generators never trip :scope-excluded and never HARD-hold; :flag-content-concern ALWAYS escalates to human sign-off and is never a member of any phase's :auto set, at any phase (two independent layers agree: tvbroadcastops.governor's own always-escalate-ops AND tvbroadcastops.phase's own phase table); real langgraph-clj StateGraph (intake->advise->govern->decide->commit|hold|request-approval) with interrupt-before #{:request-approval} for human-in-the-loop resume, not a stub; fully portable .cljc with no JVM-only interop anywhere in src/ (mock-only advisor); 40 tests / 119 assertions green, independently re-verified against a fresh clone; clj-kondo 0 errors / 0 warnings; registry.edn's own \"6020\" -> :implemented change (adding the previously-absent :maturity key explicitly -- this entry had NO :maturity key before this edit, resolving to :blueprint only via the (:repo industry) fallback in maturity-of; :repo/:business-id were already correct and left unchanged [:business-id \"cloud-itonami-6020\" already matched the repo's own blueprint.edn :itonami.blueprint/id], as was :required-technologies/:operating-states -- a deliberately minimal, exact-block diff) landed via a Contents-API single-file PUT (sha-checked optimistic concurrency, immediately re-fetched fresh content before the PUT per this fleet's hot-contention discipline, exact-block edit only verified via a before/after diff window PLUS sample-verified against 5913/6310/3512 entries also intact, no mojibake detected, landed on the first attempt); superproject ADR-2645173414 (com-junkawasaki/root, 90-docs/adr/2645173414-cloud-itonami-isic-6020-tv-broadcasting-coverage.md/.edn)) is also :implemented"
    (is (= :implemented (industry/maturity "6020"))))
  (testing "cloud-itonami-isic-6010 (Radio broadcasting -- a PRE-EXISTING repository already at :blueprint tier [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md/CONTRIBUTING.md/GOVERNANCE.md/LICENSE/README.md/SECURITY.md/blueprint.edn/docs/ only, from an earlier bulk-scaffolding pass, no deps.edn/src/test] -- this work (this session's own, not the concurrent-sibling stub it replaces) ADDED the missing deps.edn/src/test module set on top of that existing boilerplate rather than re-scaffolding, docs kept not recreated; identity ({:id \"6010\" :name \"Radio broadcasting\"}) independently re-verified against a fresh clone before any work began, per this fleet's ID/name-mismatch caution; radioops.* module (BroadcastOpsAdvisor ⊣ BroadcastOpsGovernor, radio-broadcasting OPERATIONS COORDINATION actor, NOT direct on-air-content authority and NOT emergency-alert-broadcast authority) mirroring cloud-itonami-isic-5813's [Publishing of newspapers, journals and periodicals] verified pressops.* advisor/governor/phase/operation/store/sim module shape module-for-module (radioops.* in place of pressops.*, station in place of publication); closed four-op allowlist, all :effect :propose (:log-broadcast-record/:schedule-broadcast-operation/:flag-content-concern/:coordinate-equipment-maintenance); THREE HARD governor checks, all permanent and un-overridable by any human approval -- station-unverified (target station/license record must exist AND be independently :registered?/:verified? in the store before any proposal for it may commit or escalate, re-derived from the store every time, never from proposal self-report), effect-not-propose, and scope-exclusion (folds in op-not-allowed) that permanently blocks any proposal touching finalization of an on-air-content decision or an emergency-alert-broadcast decision, per ADR-2607152500's Wave 4 person-facing-service guardrail; scope-excluded-terms are deliberately phrased as the finalization/execution ACTION or its decision-outcome noun phrase (\"on-air content decision\", \"emergency alert broadcast decision\", \"finalize the on-air content\"), never a bare noun (\"content\"/\"broadcast\"/\"emergency\"), avoiding this fleet's own known self-tripping bug class, with a dedicated regression test (default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion in advisor_test.clj) asserting all four default proposal generators never trip :scope-excluded; :flag-content-concern ALWAYS escalates to human sign-off and is never a member of any phase's :auto set, at any phase (two independent layers agree: radioops.governor's own always-escalate-ops AND radioops.phase's own phase table, exercised directly by a dedicated flag-content-concern-never-in-any-phase-auto-set structural-invariant test); real langgraph-clj StateGraph (intake->advise->govern->decide->commit|hold|request-approval) with interrupt-before #{:request-approval} for human-in-the-loop resume, not a stub; fully portable .cljc with no JVM-only interop anywhere in src/ (mock-only advisor); 45 tests / 126 assertions green, independently re-verified against a fresh clone; clj-kondo 0 errors / 0 warnings; registry.edn's own \"6010\" -> :implemented change (adding the previously-absent :maturity key explicitly -- this entry had NO :maturity key before this edit, resolving to :blueprint only via the (:repo industry) fallback in maturity-of; :repo/:business-id were already correct and left unchanged [:business-id \"cloud-itonami-6010\" matches the same bare, non--isic- convention independently confirmed on sibling cloud-itonami-isic-6020/4911/4912], as was :required-technologies/:optional-technologies/:operating-states -- a deliberately minimal, exact-block diff) landed via a Contents-API single-file PUT (sha-checked optimistic concurrency, immediately re-fetched fresh content before the PUT per this fleet's hot-contention discipline, exact-block edit only verified via an exact old/new substring occurrence count PLUS sample-verified against 4912/6020/3512/6310/5621 entries also intact, no mojibake detected, tier count already correctly re-synced by a concurrent sibling agent's own edit and left untouched by this edit); superproject ADR-2641000000 (com-junkawasaki/root, 90-docs/adr/2641000000-cloud-itonami-isic-6010-radio-broadcasting-coverage.md/.edn)) is also :implemented"
