  (testing "cloud-itonami-isic-4912 (Freight rail transport, an UNUSUAL case in this fleet's own history like sibling cloud-itonami-isic-5221 above -- NOT a fresh scaffold: `gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-4912` confirmed a PRE-EXISTING repo already at :blueprint tier (CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md/CONTRIBUTING.md/GOVERNANCE.md/LICENSE/README.md/SECURITY.md/blueprint.edn/docs/ only, from an earlier bulk-scaffolding pass, no deps.edn/src/test) -- this work ADDED the missing deps.edn/src/test module set on top of that existing boilerplate rather than re-scaffolding; identity ({:id \"4912\" :name \"Freight rail transport\"}) independently re-verified against a fresh clone before any work began, per this fleet's ID/name-mismatch caution -- unambiguous, no truncation; distinct from siblings cloud-itonami-isic-4911 [passenger rail, promoted separately by a concurrent sibling agent, corroborated above] and cloud-itonami-isic-4920 [road freight, already :implemented] -- freight rail economic regulation is frequently handled by a different regulator than passenger rail, and carries its own hazardous-materials-by-rail transport regime not applicable to road/parcel hazmat rules, per this repo's own README `Scope note`; railfreight.* module (RailFreight-LLM ⊣ Rail Freight Governor, freight-rail OPERATIONS COORDINATION actor, NOT the dispatcher, NOT the track-safety authority, and NOT rolling-stock/locomotive control) mirroring cloud-itonami-isic-4920's [Community Freight Transport] verified governed-actor architecture (langgraph StateGraph + independent Governor + Phase 0->3 rollout) -- closed four-op allowlist, all :effect :propose literally (a separate :action key carries the concrete SSoT mutation) (:log-shipment-record/:schedule-service-operation/:flag-track-safety-concern/:coordinate-maintenance); TEN HARD governor checks, all permanent and un-overridable by any human approval -- effect-not-:propose, op-not-allowlisted, action-not-allowlisted, scope-exclusion (structura