  (testing "cloud-itonami-isic-0128 (Growing of spices, aromatic, drug and pharmaceutical crops, fresh scaffold -- confirmed no prior repository existed at either the stale gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-A0128 placeholder (never populated) or the real cloud-itonami org target, via three independent methods (REST gh api repeated 404, GraphQL gh repo view \"Could not resolve to a Repository\", search API total_count 0) before any work began; identity ({:id \"0128\" :name \"Growing of spices, aromatic, drug and pharmaceutical crops\"}) independently verified against a fresh clone before any work began, per this fleet's ID/name-mismatch caution -- unambiguous, no truncation; a separate, coarser-granularity {:id \"012\" ...} 3-digit group entry left untouched; Wave 3 (production/robotics, ADR-2607121000) target -- this promotion closes out Wave 3's LAST genuine implementation gap (Wave 3 was otherwise already complete apart from two deliberately-excluded sensitive classes unrelated to this one: 2520 weapons, 3040 military vehicles); REGULATORY-COMPLIANCE-SENSITIVE domain distinct from those two permanently-excluded classes -- ISIC 0128 covers both entirely mundane spice/aromatic crops (black pepper, vanilla, cinnamon, peppermint) AND licit drug/pharmaceutical-precursor crop cultivation (licensed opium poppy for pharmaceutical morphine production, licensed coca leaf for pharmaceutical/traditional use in the few jurisdictions where this is legal, licensed medicinal cannabis), never flagged for permanent exclusion but requiring a real guardrail; SpiceCrop Advisor \u22a3 Spice/Aromatic/Drug-and-Pharmaceutical-Crop Operations Governor FARM OPERATIONS COORDINATION actor (spicecrop.* namespace) mirroring cloud-itonami-isic-0129's [Growing of other perennial crops] verified module shape module-for-module (spicecrop.* in place of perennial.*, crop-category cultivation-license/quota-tracking/harvest-quota checks in place of crop-operation-type applicator-license/sprayer-calibration/PHI/REI/wind/buffer checks); closed four-op allowlist, all :effect :propose (:log-harvest-record/:schedule-farm-operation/:flag-compliance-concern/:coordinate-supply-order); ELEVEN HARD governor checks, all permanent and un-overridable by any human approval -- farm-lot-not-registered (applies across ALL FOUR allowed ops), no-spec-basis, evidence-incomplete, cultivation-license-expired/quota-tracking-lapsed/harvest-quota-exceeded (each only for controlled-substance crop categories, skipped cleanly -- never fabricated -- for non-controlled spice/aromatic crop categories), compliance-flag-unresolved, already-logged, effect-not-propose, op-not-allowed, and the flagship cultivation-license-or-diversion-clearance-blocked check that permanently blocks any proposal covertly requesting to finalize a controlled-substance cultivation-license approval/renewal or a diversion-control-compliance clearance via explicit boolean :value flags (:finalize-cultivation-license-approval?/:finalize-cultivation-license-renewal?/:finalize-diversion-control-clearance?) -- this actor coordinates FARM OPERATIONS LOGISTICS ONLY, never grants or renews any controlled-substance cultivation license itself; scope-excluded terms are deliberately phrased as the finalization/execution ACTION via explicit structural :value flags rather than any free-text scan, so this actor's own default advisor rationale text (which legitimately and routinely discusses \"license\"/\"clearance\"/\"diversion\" as ordinary compliance disclaimer language) can never self-trip it -- this fleet's own known self-tripping bug class avoided from the start, verified by a dedicated regression test (default-mock-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion-test in governor_test.cljc) asserting all four of spicecrop.advisor/default-mock-proposals clear the governor with :cultivation-license-or-diversion-clearance-blocked and :op-not-allowed both absent from violations; :flag-compliance-concern ALWAYS escalates to human sign-off and is never a member of any phase's auto-commit set, at any phase (two independent layers agree: spicecrop.governor's own always-escalate-ops AND its own phase-auto-ops map, the latter exercised directly by a dedicated flag-compliance-concern-never-in-any-phase-auto-set structural test using a dedicated auto-eligible-at-phase? helper); :log-harvest-record (the one real actuation event this actor performs) likewise always escalates and is never a member of any phase's auto-commit set; a :coordinate-supply-order above a 5000 USD cost threshold also always escalates; governor-keyword collision check performed pre-landing (:spice-crop-governor, gh api search/code zero hits across the cloud-itonami org before finalizing); fully portable .cljc with no JVM-only interop anywhere in src/ (mock-only advisor); 45 tests / 198 assertions green (clojure -M:test), independently re-verified against a fresh clone; clj-kondo 0 errors / 0 warnings; registry.edn's own \"0128\" -> :implemented change (:repo/:business-id de-placeholdered from gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-A0128 -> cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-0128, :maturity :spec->:implemented, :required-technologies/:optional-technologies/:operating-states left unchanged, already correctly registered) landed via a Contents-API single-file PUT (sha-checked optimistic concurrency against a freshly re-fetched git-trees/blobs API snapshot immediately before the PUT, exact-block edit only verified via an exact old/new substring occurrence count of 1 PLUS sample-verified against 0127/0129/3512 entries and the untouched 012[group] entry also intact, no mojibake detected, landed on the first attempt); superproject ADR-2780000128 (com-junkawasaki/root, 90-docs/adr/2780000128-cloud-itonami-isic-0128-spice-pharmaceutical-crop-coverage.md/.edn)) is also :implemented"
