, and scope exclusion (an op outside the closed four-op allowlist, OR content directly finalizing a welfare/aid-eligibility determination, directly executing field/production work on a household's behalf, or suspending/terminating a household's programme enrollment -- phrased as finalization/execution ACTION phrases like \"finalize the eligibility determination\"/\"directly perform the harvest\"/\"suspend programme enrollment\", not the bare nouns \"eligibility\"/\"harvest\"/\"enrollment\" alone); this build actually HIT the fleet's known bare-noun self-tripping bug during its own development, not merely guarded against it in the abstract -- the initial :coordinate-programme-support default rationale literally contained the substring \"\u7d66\u4ed8\u8cc7\u683c\u306e\u78ba\u5b9a\" (\"finalization of aid eligibility\"), also one of the governor's own scope-excluded terms, caught by a pre-test programmatic scan of every default proposal against the term list and fixed by rewording the rationale (never by weakening the term list); a dedicated regression test (default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion, parameterized over all four allowlisted ops) guards against recurrence, alongside legitimate-food-security-concern-is-not-scope-excluded; flag-food-security-concern ALWAYS escalates to human sign-off and is never a member of any phase's :auto set, at any phase (two independent layers agree: hhproductionops.governor's own always-escalate-ops and hhproductionops.phase's own phase table); coordinate-programme-support above a $250 estimated-cost threshold also always escalates regardless of confidence; fully portable .cljc with no JVM-only interop anywhere in src/ (mock-only advisor); 45 tests / 128 assertions green, independently re-verified against a fresh clone (both clojure -M:test and clojure -M:dev:test, identical result, plus fresh kotoba-lang/langgraph and kotoba-lang/langchain siblings); clj-kondo 0 errors / 0 warnings; registry.edn's own \"9810\"