rridable by any human approval) -- op-not-allowed (closed allowlist enforced independently of the advisor's own routing), effect-not-propose (every proposal's :effect is HARD-required to be the literal keyword :propose, no domain-specific mutation-effect keyword exists in this domain by design), scope-exclusion-sail-clearance (permanent block on directly finalizing a sail-clearance/weather-hold/maritime-safety override), certification-incomplete (the sailing's own vessel/voyage certification record must be independently verified+registered, re-derived from the sailing's own store record every time, never from the proposal's own self-report; applies to all ops except log-voyage-record itself), imo-number-invalid (honest reapplication of cloud-itonami-isic-5020's own SOLAS/IMO A.600(15) 7-digit check-digit scheme -- applies to every SOLAS-class ship, not only tankers), no-spec-basis (per-jurisdiction passenger-vessel safety-certification catalog, JPN/USA/GBR/NOR seeded, honest coverage reporting), and already-scheduled (dedicated :scheduled? boolean, never a :status value); scope-excluded terms are deliberately phrased as the finalization/execution ACTION ('finalize the sail-clearance override', 'override the weather-hold', 'clear the vessel to sail despite the fault', 'authorize departure despite the reported fault'), never a bare noun ('safety'/'clearance'/'weather-hold' alone) -- this fleet's own known bare-noun self-tripping bug class avoided from the start, since :schedule-sailing-operation's own rationale, for a sailing with a reported fault or active weather hold, necessarily discusses those exact conditions, and :flag-maritime-safety-concern's entire purpose is to surface them; a dedicated regression test (default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion in scope_exclusion_test.cljc) independently confirms every allowlisted op's own default (clean) advisor-generated proposal text, across all six demo sailings (including the fault-reported+weather-hold-active one), never trips :scope-exclusion-sail-clearance, alongside a direct-unit-test file (governor_test.cljc) proving the check is not vacuous (a hand-crafted proposal containing each phrase verbatim IS hard-blocked); :flag-maritime-safety-concern ALWAYS escalates to human sign-off and is never a member of any phase's :auto set, at any phase, and is not even writable until phase 3 (two independent layers agree: ferry.governor's own high-stakes set and ferry.phase's own phase table); real langgraph-clj StateGraph (intake->advise->govern->decide->commit|hold|request-approval) with interrupt-before #{:request-approval} for human-in-the-loop resume, not a stub; the NEW ferry.store DatomicStore adopts kotoba-lang/langchain-store (ADR-2607141600) as its field-spec entity-store seam rather than hand-rolling enc/dec, per skill build-actor's current guidance (a deliberate departure from cloud-itonami-isic-5020, which predates that library); ALL source AND test files are .cljc (not .clj), including a portable-cljs-test-runner + :cljs deps.edn alias, per this workspace's cljs-first mandate; fully portable with no JVM-only interop anywhere in src/ (mock-only + optional llm-advisor); 46 tests / 272 assertions green, independently re-verified against a fresh clone; clj-kondo 0 errors / 0 warnings; registry.edn's own \"5011\" -> :implemented change (adding the previously-absent :maturity key explicitly -- this entry had NO :maturity key before this edit, resolving to :blueprint only via the (:repo industry) fallback in maturity-of; :repo/:business-id/:required-technologies/:optional-technologies were already correct and left unchanged) landed via a Contents-API single-file PUT (sha-checked optimistic concurrency, a prefix/suffix scan confirmed a single contiguous changed region matching only the intended :maturity insertion, sample-verified against 3512/6310/5020/5221/9810 entries also intact, no mojibake detected, landed on the first attempt), commit 23db6561e48ed605f979