  (testing "cloud-itonami-isic-8110 (Combined facilities support activities -- final batch of Wave 2's [coordination/logistics/trade, ADR-2607121000] remaining 4-digit gaps; fresh scaffold, `gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-8110` confirmed 404 before any work began; identity ({:id \"8110\" :name \"Combined facilities support activities\"}) independently verified against a fresh clone before any work began, per this fleet's ID/name-mismatch caution -- unambiguous, no truncation; a separate, coarser-granularity {:id \"811\" ...} 3-digit group entry (same name, :repo nil) left untouched; distinct from sibling ISIC 8129 [Other building and industrial cleaning activities, built concurrently in this same batch, separate actor, separate governor -- checked and confirmed no namespace/governor-keyword collision]; NEW sub-sector for this batch -- facility/support services, not transport, not retail: a single contractor bundling cleaning, security, maintenance and grounds-keeping for a building/campus under ONE contract; FacilitiesSupportAdvisor ⊣ FacilitiesSupportGovernor combined-facilities-support OPERATIONS COORDINATION actor (facilitiesops.* namespace) mirroring cloud-itonami-isic-4719's [Other retail sale in non-specialized stores] verified advisor/governor/phase/operation/store/sim module shape module-for-module (facilitiesops.* in place of merchandiseops.*, facility-contract/supplier registration in place of store/vendor registration); closed four-op allowlist, all :effect :propose (:log-service-record/:schedule-service-operation/:coordinate-supply-order/:flag-facility-concern); FOUR HARD governor checks, all permanent and un-overridable by any human approval -- facility-unverified (the target facility's combined-services contract record must be independently :registered?/:verified? in the store before any proposal for it may commit or escalate, re-derived from the store every time, never from proposal self-report), supplier-unverified (for :coordinate-supply-order only, the named supplier must independently resolve to a :registered?/:verified? supplier record, the same ground-truth discipline reapplied to a facility-supply-chain counterparty), effect-not-propose, and scope-exclusion (folds in op-not-allowed) that permanently blocks any proposal touching directly finalizing a building-access-credential grant or revocation (issuing/activating/revoking/deactivating a keycard/badge/door-code) or directly overriding/bypassing/disabling an emergency-response protocol -- this actor's own closed op-allowlist structurally never includes any op that could finalize either, on top of this independent defense-in-depth scope-exclusion check; scope-excluded terms are deliberately phrased as the finalization/execution ACTION (\"granted building access\", \"revoked the access credential\", \"overrode the emergency response protocol\"), never a bare noun (\"access\"/\"credential\"/\"security\"/\"emergency\") -- this namespace's own :flag-facility-concern default proposal legitimately discusses security-incident/maintenance-hazard/access-control concerns, so a bare-noun term list would have self-tripped this actor's own core happy path on every single run -- avoided from the start, verified by a dedicated regression test (default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion in governor_test.clj) asserting all four default proposal generators never trip :scope-excluded or :op-not-allowed, plus a companion sanity test (out-of-scope-injection-still-trips-scope-exclusion) confirming the check is not accidentally a no-op; :flag-facility-concern ALWAYS escalates to human sign-off and is never a member of any phase's :auto set, at any phase (two independent layers agree: facilitiesops.governor's own always-escalate-ops AND facilitiesops.phase's own phase table, the latter exercised directly by a dedicated facility-concern-never-in-any-phase-auto-set structural test); a :coordinate-supply-order above a $2000 estimated-cost threshold also always escalates; governor keyword :facilities-support-governor and namespace facilitiesops checked for fleet collision via `gh api search/code` (both zero results), specifically including sibling ISIC 8129 built concurrently in this same batch; real langgraph-clj StateGraph (intake->advise->govern->decide->commit|hold|request-approval) with interrupt-before #{:request-approval} for human-in-the-loop resume, not a stub; fully portable .cljc with no JVM-only interop anywhere in src/ (mock-only advisor); 57 tests / 168 assertions green (clojure -M:test), independently re-verified against a fresh clone; clj-kondo 0 errors / 0 warnings; clojure -M:run (facilitiesops.sim demo) walked all scenarios (phase-1 approval-gated commit, phase-3 auto-commit for the three non-safety/low-cost ops, always-escalating facility-concern flag, always-escalating over-threshold supply order, and five HARD-hold scenarios: unregistered facility, unverified facility, unverified supplier, non-:propose effect, scope-excluded content) without error; registry.edn's own \"8110\" -> :implemented change (:repo/:business-id de-placeholdered from the stale gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-N8110 target to cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-8110, :maturity :spec -> :implemented, :operating-states updated from the stale intake/register/match/dispatch/follow-up/audit placeholder to match the real langgraph-clj node sequence; :required-technologies left unchanged, already domain-appropriate) landed via a Contents-API single-file PUT direct to main (sha-checked optimistic concurrency, re-fetched fresh content four times immediately before the PUT after three prior 409s from concurrent sibling churn per this fleet's hot-contention discipline, exact-block edit only verified via an exact old/new substring occurrence count of 1 PLUS a prefix/suffix single-contiguous-diff-region check PLUS sample-verified against 811[group]/8129/4719/6310 entries also intact, no mojibake detected); superproject ADR-2740008110 (com-junkawasaki/root, 90-docs/adr/2740008110-cloud-itonami-isic-8110-combined-facilities-support-coverage.md/.edn, merged via server-side merge) promoted :spec -> :implemented"
